{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["ואביו שמר את הדבר — What need is there to write this? Rather, when the news came to him and he did not believe his sons that he was alive — וירא ישראל את העגלות אשר שלח פרעה, for they were not sent except by order of the king, as it is written there עגלות על פי פרעה — then he believed by means of the dreams, which prove that his destiny was to be a ruler. And these wagons come by way of kingship and dominion, and on account of this he said: רב עוד יוסף בני חי. For it would be a great wonder how he believed after seeing his cloak soaked in blood — just as Yitzhak was shaken over Yaakov, because he found hair on the smooth part of his neck."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:25.932634251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}